---
code: cli-shim-dir-unwritable
when-fires: the --shim-dir materialization edge could not create or write the per-run PATH shims. cli/main.rs. {path} and PASSTHROUGH {detail}.
why: 274 section 5: shim materialization is session-establishment I/O the wrapped probe needs, so a failure is loud rather than a silently shim-less run that would resolve the wrong guest.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cli-shim-dir-unwritable && mise run loom:promote -- cli-shim-dir-unwritable`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cli-shim-dir-unwritable` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
